id:                     DRAFT-shyaml-codeload-generated-python-metadata
trigger_tool:           python|pip|conan|git
phase:                  configuration|installation
error_signature:        Missing version information.*autogen\.sh|Didn't find a git repository.*no tags found|%%version%%
severity:               2
category:               python, packaging, versioning, build-system
match_keywords:         codeload, setup.py, autogen.sh, git describe, %%version%%, d2to1, source archive, shyaml
prescan_pattern:        %%version%%.*autogen\.sh|git describe --tags.*setup\.py
prescan_globs:          setup.py, setup.cfg, autogen.sh, *.py

title:                  Legacy Python setup.py templates can require Git history absent from codeload archives

root_cause:             Some legacy Python projects leave release metadata as %%version%% templates and invoke autogen.sh from setup.py when the tokens remain. The generator uses git describe --tags, but GitHub codeload archives contain source files without .git or tag refs. Running setup.py/pip against that archive therefore fails before installation even though the pure-Python module itself is usable. Shyaml 0.6.2 and vaab/colour 0.1.5 share this .package/autogen.sh pattern.
affected_scope:         Legacy pure-Python packages whose source archive leaves setup metadata templates for a VCS-dependent generator; not normal PyPI sdists or projects whose release archive already includes generated metadata.
verification_cmd:       Inspect setup.py/setup.cfg for %%version%% and the fallback autogen.sh; extract the pinned codeload archive, verify .git is absent, then run the package's documented setup.py --version or pip install command and record the missing-repository error.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           pinned-release-metadata-and-direct-module-staging
rec_description:        Pin the upstream tag archive and SHA-256, substitute only release-derived placeholders from the Conan recipe version, and stage the pure Python module plus an equivalent relocatable CLI entry point without invoking a VCS-dependent autogen step.
rec_command:            python3 -c "from shyaml import __version__; assert __version__ == '0.6.2'"; then run the installed CLI and the upstream doctest/docshtest suite
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      materialize-tagged-vcs-metadata
fallback_description:   If setup.py must run, supply a pinned Git checkout with the exact tag or create the minimal generated metadata from the verified tag; never substitute a floating branch.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       git clone.*main|master|autogen\.sh.*git describe.*ignore|%%version%%.*ship
forbid_1_reason:        A floating checkout changes the source coordinate, while ignoring the generator failure can leave runtime version output unreleased or installation incomplete.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package is not reproducible at the requested tag, or the installed CLI reports an unknown version and lacks generated metadata.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [DRAFT-libcork-0.9.0-version-sh-git-describe, DRAFT-libfirm-1.22.0-makefile-version-header-tarball]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

